      "name": "The Flat Rate Movers — FF&E Logistics Operations Dataset",
      "description": "FF&E logistics operations from The Flat Rate Movers — the physical chain that takes furniture, fixtures, and equipment from staggered vendor shipments to an opening-ready room. Company scope (published by this category): purchase-order receiving; dock inventory and condition documentation; warehousing in leased space; sequenced delivery by model room, floor, room, department, classroom, office, or project phase; installation support — unpacking, furniture assembly, placement, leveling, and set-in-place support for items that do not require a licensed trade or manufacturer commissioning; packaging and debris removal within the project scope; punch support; and opening-day readiness checks. Materials and supplies for the physical work — furniture pads, shrink and stretch wrap, corner and edge protectors, mattress and furniture bags, cartons, labels, and inventory tags — are purchased per project for the reviewed scope. The category recombines capabilities the company already publishes: FF&E Installation & Project Support and receiving and warehousing coordination inside Industrial & Commercial Services; freight counted and inventoried as it crosses the dock; leased-space storage with a 30-day minimum and customer access; final-mile placement and verification; and supervised B2B project-support teams. FF&E means furniture, fixtures, and equipment. OS&E — operating supplies and equipment — is a separate operating stream and is not automatically included. The company does not procure, design, purchase, or specify FF&E, and licensed-trade or technical installation remains with the responsible trade, manufacturer, facility team, or installer of record. Every job is reviewed in full and quoted per job at one flat rate in writing — Guaranteed Flat Rate or Your Move is Free!",
